          "content": "A **collision** occurs in a hash table when two different keys produce the same index (hash value) after being processed by the hash function. Since a single slot in the underlying array cannot hold two distinct pieces of data simultaneously, the hash table must have a strategy to handle this.\n\nThere are two primary categories of collision resolution: **Open Addressing** and **Separate Chaining**.\n\n---\n\n### Method 1: Separate Chaining (The \"Bucket\" Approach)\nIn separate chaining, each slot in the hash table array does not hold a single item, but rather a pointer to a **linked list** (or another data",
